# SFT execution status v0.109

2026-09-23. Local implementation of the fixed full-size entry and source/control
staging is complete and tested. **Execution is still closed; Gate 5 is not
complete.** No checkpoint/tokenizer payload or dataset was read. No S3 request,
remote action, native installation, GPU operation, commit or push occurred.

## Completed

- Fixed entry script: worker/runtime check before reads, self/helper/source/control
  pins, exact eight-body header, fresh private source copies, inert `lumi`
  namespace, repeated pure resource validation and one private one-shot entry
  call. Its returned summary matches the existing guardian protocol.
- Source/control-only addon: exact owned-rootfs preflight, absent fixed
  destinations, prepaid content bounds and taint-on-started-failure. It creates
  no checkpoint/tokenizer/output/mountpoint siblings or payload files.
- Worker dependency manifest: **39 source files, 667,545 bytes**, including lazy
  imports and reviewed finite dynamic model-module imports. The original
  initializer remains authenticated but is not executed; arbitrary dynamic
  dependency completeness or native source admission is not claimed.

Public script `main()` returns 2 without dispatch or output. The public addon
installer remains `host_guard_not_bound`. Private functions are future admitted
worker/parent targets, not permission supplied by a flag or hash.

## Verification and output safety

**491 unique tests pass on both CPython 3.11.15 and 3.13.7**, with no failures,
errors or skips: 52 new script tests, 21 addon tests, 11 source-closure tests and
407 prior regressions. The integration case uses actual code bindings with
generated 4B integer-only metadata; it does not allocate or import model weights.

Ruff passes all five new Python files. Source/addon review identified a stdout
gap: dependency output must not enter the report socket. The private adapter now
redirects stdout to the bootstrap's null stderr during import/execution and
flushes captured Python buffers before restoration. Failed initial/final flush
keeps the sink selected and closes the saved report handle, without retry.
Root implemented the final flush correction and reran the full regression set.
Arbitrary native C-stdio buffering is still not proven contained.

The explicit addon-content ceiling is 5,191,700 bytes; worker setup reads are
bounded at 9,386,004 bytes and private source-copy writes at 4,194,304 bytes.
These are separate from model-import counters. They exclude implicit Python
loader reads, metadata, OS/dependency writes and other setup/acquisition work,
and depend on independently enforced source/writer premises.

All 21 readiness, nine entry-development and six lifecycle-development bindings
match; all 78 prior qualified sources and 39 new worker source rows match their
hashes. Earlier evidence is unchanged. Tracked and staged diffs remain empty;
the new files are local and unpushed.

