## Remaining before native execution

The next local work is cumulative native-write enforcement and bounded
setup/OS/scratch/report handling, plus the full-size input/output layout.
An executable dispatcher needs a permanent diagnostic sink and dedicated
bounded report descriptor before `main` can be enabled. The partial containment
limitation recorded in v0.108 also remains; this step does not erase it.

After that, the successor still needs bounded Linux qualification and the
existing host/runtime/source admission, immutable backing or writer exclusion,
mount/resource readback, combined budgets and exact real-import authorization.
No extra policy gate is introduced, and no earlier gate is marked complete
merely because synthetic tests passed.

The previously bound S3-backed pretrained checkpoint remains the intended base;
current S3 availability was not checked. Training and production stay disabled.
GPU is not needed for the next local implementation work.
